This repository builds and sets up Rusty MCLA, the unofficial PC port of
Midnight Club: Los Angeles written in Rust, on ARM64 Linux handhelds:
https://github.com/holdmysocks/rusty-mcla, GPL-3.0-only. upstream.json pins
the commit it is built from and patches/ holds the changes made to it; every
release carries the patched source (RustyMCLA-source.tar.gz) beside the ARM64
build, and the build carries upstream's THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.

The install downloads ffmpeg from https://github.com/BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds
(GPL) on the device to convert the disc's audio and films; it is never
shipped here.

tools/steam-art draws the Steam artwork with the Anton font
(https://github.com/googlefonts/AntonFont, SIL Open Font License 1.1, see
tools/steam-art/fonts/OFL.txt) over screenshots the game takes of itself on
the device.

The launcher and the Steam scripts come from the Road Trip Adventure and FIFA
Street ARM64 ports (https://github.com/Ken5998/road-trip-arm64,
https://github.com/Ken5998/fifa-street-arm64) by the same author.

This is an unofficial fan project, not affiliated with, authorised or
endorsed by Rockstar Games or Take-Two Interactive. No game files are
included: the player uses their own Xbox 360 disc image of Midnight Club: Los
Angeles, Complete Edition.
